==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|διαστολή||separation, drawing asunder|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|διά||apart|tr=diá|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|στέλλειν||send|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{physiology}} The [[relaxation]] and [[dilation]] of the [[heart]] chambers, between contractions, during which they fill with blood.
# {{prosody}} To lengthen a vowel or syllable beyond its typical length.

